// character_overrides.json: hand-authored personalities for Calradia Remembers.
//
// Enable in Mod Options -> Calradia Remembers -> Character -> "Use custom traits".
// When on, each entry below REPLACES that NPC's five vanilla personality traits, so the prompt's
// derived persona, the trait-derived features (kinks, and so on), and the campaign AI all read your
// values. Turning the toggle off restores the vanilla traits.
//
// HOW TO ADD A CHARACTER:
//   1. Remove the // from each line of the example block inside the [ ] brackets below.
//   2. Edit the values to taste, keeping the block between the [ ] brackets.
//   3. For more than one character, separate each { } block with a comma.
//   4. Save, then run cr.reload_lore from the console (Alt and ~), or reload your save.
//
// FIELDS (per entry):
//   "hero"        display name to match (case-insensitive)
//   "id"          OPTIONAL StringId, to tell apart two NPCs who share a name
//   "valor", "honor", "mercy", "generosity", "calculating"   each -2..+2; omit one to keep its vanilla value
//   "backstory"   OPTIONAL. WHO THEY ARE AND HOW THEY SOUND: voice, temperament, manner, speech quirks.
//                 It colours how they SPEAK. It does not decide what they DO: conduct follows their traits.
//   "conviction"  OPTIONAL. WHAT THEY HOLD TRUE, AND THEREFORE WHAT THEY WANT. This one moves what they
//                 DECIDE, not just how they talk. It may be FALSE, and that is the point: a lord who believes
//                 he pulls the strings of your clan, a companion who believes she is secretly a necromancer.
//                 They act on it. If it would ruin them were it known, they hide it, and hiding it becomes a
//                 motive of its own.
//                 Three limits: it grants no powers (he may hoard bones, he may not raise the dead), it
//                 imports no lore from outside the world you are playing, and it cannot bend the world to
//                 suit it. A belief can make them WANT a thing. Only deeds decide whether they get it.
//   "orientation" OPTIONAL. A human word for the NPC's sexual orientation: straight/hetero, bi/bisexual,
//                 gay/lesbian/homo, bi-curious, pan/pansexual, ace/asexual. Overrides the roll, e.g. to
//                 enable a same-sex romance the roll blocked. The cr.orientation console command sets it
//                 live for the current session; put it here to make the change permanent.
//   "kinks"       OPTIONAL, Hardcore adult content level only. A list of kink names that LOCKS this NPC's
//                 intimate profile to exactly that list, instead of the usual roll (or whatever cr.add_kink
//                 / cr.remove_kink last left it at). Survives cr.reload_lore and a save reload; this is how
//                 you stage a captive scene or a romance with specific kinks and have them stick. An empty
//                 list ("kinks": []) is a deliberate lock to NO kinks. Omit the field entirely to leave the
//                 NPC's kinks alone (rolled, or whatever the console last set).
//                 Valid names (case-insensitive): Dominance, Submission, SwitchTendencies, Sadism,
//                 Masochism, BondageGiving, BondageReceiving, Roleplay, PowerImbalance, Exhibitionism,
//                 Voyeurism, Possessiveness, PublicAffection, OrgasmControl, Chastity, FreeUse, Degradation,
//                 Objectification, PetPlay, Praise, ImpactPlay, SensoryDeprivation, FearPlay, MasterSlave,
//                 Breeding, Training, CorruptionKink, Prize. (Also listed live by the cr.kinks console command.)
//
//   "preferences" OPTIONAL. A list of romantic-preference names that LOCKS how this character loves, instead of
//                 the usual roll. This is how you write ONE polyamorous character into a strictly monogamous
//                 culture, or one devoted romantic into a worldly one. An empty list ("preferences": []) is a
//                 deliberate lock to none; omit the field to leave the rolled preferences alone.
//                 Valid names (case-insensitive): MonogamousStrict, MonogamousFlexible, Polyamorous, Casual,
//                 Devoted, Possessive, Independent, Reserved, SlowBurn, Intense, Dominant, Submissive, Switch.
//                 NOTE: whether a character MAY be polyamorous by default comes from their culture, in
//                 jealousy_cultures.json, not from their Honor trait. This field overrides that for one person.
//
//   "loves"       OPTIONAL, Hardcore only. The gestures this character particularly loves in bed, replacing the
//   "dislikes"    roll; and the ones they dislike (refused plainly or with an unease you can read, and imposed
//                 anyway they cost personal regard). An empty list is a deliberate lock to none; omit to keep the
//                 roll. A gesture in both counts as loved. Valid names: kissing, oral_giving, oral_receiving,
//                 anal_giving, anal_receiving, on_top, beneath, from_behind, hands_and_fingers, rough_handling,
//                 dirty_talk, named from the character's side (oral_giving: their mouth on their partner). Also
//                 listed by the cr.acts console command.
//
[
